    <div class="break">
      <figure id="cb-debt" style="margin:0">
        <div class="plate-head">
          <div class="t">
            <h3>India's foreign debt has grown with the economy, and most of it is long-term</h3>
            <div class="sub">External debt as on 31 March each year since 1991, US$ billion: the total and its largest parts.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="plate-val"><div class="v acc" id="pv-debt">–</div><div class="c">{DEBT}</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="frame">
          <div class="plotzone" id="plot-debt"><div class="cb-tip"></div></div>
          <div class="plotfoot">
            <span class="src">Source: RBI, India's external debt as on end-March (DBIE report 563). Commercial borrowing includes companies' foreign loans and bonds and foreign investors' holdings of Indian debt; NRI deposits count only those maturing in over a year.</span>
