            <span class="mk">How to read this</span>
            <p>Who owes the debt matters as much as how much there is. Government debt abroad is mostly long-term: loans from the World Bank and friendly governments, and government bonds held by foreign investors. Company debt is commercial: if the rupee falls, a company that borrowed in dollars and earns in rupees has to find more rupees to repay.</p>
