    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Reserve Bank of India, Database on Indian Economy (DBIE), read from India Atlas's archived copy of DBIE, not fetched live from the RBI. Every external-sector table DBIE publishes is either baked into a file listed above or accounted for in the coverage ledger: copies of the same table under other DBIE menus, and the few tables DBIE serves without names for their columns. Data vintage <b id="prov-vintage">–</b>.</p>
        <p>Checked by hand against the RBI's own figures: the latest quarter's current account, the reserves in the Weekly Statistical Supplement, and the current-account ratio to GDP in RBI's press release. The checks, and every source quirk found, are recorded in the adapters and in the guide's status notes.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Method</h6>
        <p>RBI publishes amounts in US$ million; this guide shows them in US$ billion. Where several versions of a figure exist, the latest is shown and the earlier are kept. Sums over fiscal years, month-to-month changes and shares are computed by India Atlas and say so. Nothing is estimated or filled in.</p>
